Owners' association rules (RE-SVB-07)

Issuer: Dunaj Reality s. r. o. · IČO 46 891 203 · Štúrova 8, 811 02 Bratislava  

Effective: 15 January 2026 · Owner: Conveyancing desk

A block of flats is administered either by an owners' association (spoločenstvo vlastníkov) or by a professional management company under the Flat Ownership Act (zákon č. 182/1993 Z. z.).

Alterations touching common parts — enclosing a balcony, moving a load-bearing wall, adding an air-conditioning unit on the façade — need owners' consent at the majority the Act requires, plus a building authority permit.

A special contribution to the repair fund approved by the owners' meeting binds the buyer, so it must appear in the buyer's package together with the arrears statement.

House rules may restrict pets, short-term letting and commercial use; verify them before marketing a unit as an investment for short-term rental.

Never promise a buyer that association consent is a formality.

